Discs are read without a read-ahead thread.

Mednafen has two disc readers: one with a thread that reads sectors ahead of
the game, one that reads a sector when it is asked for. The second is always
used here, for the same reason as patch 0001.

--- a/src/cdrom/CDInterface.cpp
+++ b/src/cdrom/CDInterface.cpp
@@ -243,10 +243,16 @@
  //
  std::unique_ptr<CDAccess> cda(CDAccess_Open(vfs, path, image_memcache));
 
+#if defined(CHIMERA_CORE)
+ // chimera: always the reader that reads on the caller's thread. The other
+ // one reads ahead on a thread of its own, and a Chimera core is one thread.
+ return new CDInterface_ST(std::move(cda));
+#else
  if(image_memcache)
   return new CDInterface_ST(std::move(cda));
  else
   return new CDInterface_MT(std::move(cda), affinity);
+#endif
 }
 
 }
